Patient Record Management System

Module: PROG211 – Object-Oriented Programming 1
Domain: Health
Language: Python
Development environment: PyCharm

1. Project Overview

The Patient Record Management System is a simple, menu-driven Python application created for an introductory object-oriented programming assignment. It demonstrates how classes, objects, methods, and lists can be used to manage basic patient and doctor records.

This is an educational prototype only. It is not intended for real clinical use. Use fictional sample data for demonstrations and testing.

2. Features

• Register a patient
• Display all registered patients
• Search for a patient by ID
• Update a patient’s medical condition
• Register a doctor
• Display registered doctors
• Assign a doctor to a patient
• Display the patients assigned to a doctor
• Display the total number of patients
• Validate patient age and prevent duplicate patient/doctor IDs
• Prevent duplicate entries in a doctor’s patient list

3. Object-Oriented Programming Concepts

Patient class

Stores a patient’s ID, name, age, gender, medical condition, blood group, and assigned doctor.

Methods include:

• display_info() — displays a patient’s information
• update_record() — updates the patient’s medical condition
• assign_doctor() — assigns a doctor to the patient
• show_total_patients() — a class method that displays the total number of patient objects created

Doctor class

Stores a doctor’s ID, name, specialization, department, and assigned patients.

Methods include:

• display_info() — displays a doctor’s information
• add_patient() — adds a patient object to the doctor’s patient list
• display_patients() — displays the patients assigned to the doctor

Data structures and object interaction

Python lists store multiple patient and doctor objects. When a doctor is assigned to a patient, the Patient object stores the Doctor object and the Doctor object stores the Patient object in its patient list.

4. Requirements

• Python 3
• PyCharm or another Python IDE

No third-party Python packages are required.

5. How to Run the Program in PyCharm

1. Download or clone this repository to your computer.
2. Open PyCharm.
3. Choose File → Open and select the project folder.
4. Open patient_record_system.py.
5. Click the green Run button, or right-click the file and choose Run ‘patient_record_system’.
6. Use the numbered menu in the Run window. Enter a menu number when prompted.

6. Example Run

A sample interaction may look like this:

PATIENT RECORD MANAGEMENT SYSTEM
1. Add Patient
2. Display All Patients
3. Search Patient
4. Update Patient Record
5. Add Doctor
6. Display Doctors
7. Assign Doctor to Patient
8. Show Total Patients
9. Display Doctor's Patients
10. Exit
Enter your choice: 1

Enter Patient ID: P001
Enter Patient Name: John Kamara
Enter Age: 25
Enter Gender: Male
Enter Medical Condition: Malaria
Enter Blood Group: O+

Patient added successfully!

The names and details above are fictional examples. All data is held in memory while the program is running. Records are not saved after the program exits.

7. Digital Public Goods Considerations

• Open and reusable code: The Python source is organized and commented so learners can study and adapt it.
• Privacy: Demonstrations should use fictional data, not real patient records.
• Modularity: Separate classes and functions make the program easier to understand and extend.
• Accessibility: A simple text-based menu keeps the program lightweight and does not require additional libraries.

This project is a classroom prototype and does not implement production security features such as authentication, encryption, role-based access, or permanent database storage.

8. Testing

|Test|Action                         |Expected result                                  |
|----|-------------------------------|-------------------------------------------------|
|1   |Add a patient                  |Patient is added successfully                    |
|2   |Display all patients           |Registered patients are displayed                |
|3   |Search using a valid patient ID|Matching patient is displayed                    |
|4   |Search using an unknown ID     |“Patient not found” message appears              |
|5   |Update a patient’s condition   |Updated condition is used for the current session|
|6   |Add a doctor                   |Doctor is added successfully                     |
|7   |Assign a doctor to a patient   |The patient and doctor are linked                |
|8   |Display a doctor’s patients    |Assigned patients are displayed                  |
|9   |Show total patients            |Class method displays the patient count          |
|10  |Enter invalid age or menu input|A validation or error message appears            |

Run these tests yourself and record the actual results. Capture screenshots from PyCharm for the assignment evidence.

